.TH AAS-SIGN 1 2026-10-19 aas-sign
.SH NAME
aas\-sign \- sign Windows PE images with Azure Artifact Signing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aas\-sign sign
.RB [ \-\-as
.IR region : account : profile ]
.RI [ options ]
.IR file " ..."
.br
.B aas\-sign login
.RI [ region : account : profile ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B aas\-sign logout
.br
.B aas\-sign config
.IR region : account : profile
.br
.B aas\-sign config
.RB [ \-\-endpoint
.IR host ]
.RB [ \-\-account
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-\-profile
.IR name ]
.br
.B aas\-sign
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aas\-sign
signs PE images, such as EXE and DLL files,
using Azure Artifact Signing (formerly Trusted Signing),
with no local private key.
It computes each file's Authenticode SHA-256 digest,
has Azure sign it,
timestamps the signature with an RFC 3161 time-stamp authority,
and embeds the result in the file.
Files are modified in place, replacing any existing signature.
Progress and errors are written to standard error.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B sign
Sign each
.IR file .
Given several, up to
.B \-\-max\-parallel
are signed at once,
each file's output is printed as one block prefixed with its name,
and a summary follows.
A failure does not stop the remaining files.
.TP
.B login
Sign in to Microsoft Entra ID with the system web browser
(authorization code flow with PKCE),
and cache a refresh token for later
.B sign
commands.
Entra redirects the browser to a temporary listener on
.BR localhost ,
so the browser must run on the same machine.
If none opens, visit the URL printed on standard error.
A signing target, if given, is then saved as by
.BR config .
.TP
.B logout
Delete the cached refresh token.
This does not revoke it.
.TP
.B config
Save signing defaults to
.I config.json
without signing in.
A
.IR region : account : profile
argument sets all three, while
.BR \-\-endpoint ,
.BR \-\-account ,
and
.B \-\-profile
set only those given.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Signing target
A signing target is a regional endpoint, an Artifact Signing account,
and a certificate profile,
given either as one
.IR region : account : profile
tuple or with the options below, but not both.
A
.I region
without a dot expands to
.IB region \%.codesigning.azure.net\fR,
so
.B eus:contoso:release
names endpoint
.BR \%eus.codesigning.azure.net ,
account
.BR contoso ,
and profile
.BR release .
A
.I region
containing a dot is taken as the hostname itself.
.B sign
fills in any part not given from
.IR config.json ,
which
.B login
and
.B config
write.
.TP
.BI "\-\-as " region\fR:\fIaccount\fR:\fIprofile
The signing target as one tuple, for
.BR sign .
.B login
and
.B config
take it as an argument instead.
.TP
.BI \-\-endpoint " host"
Endpoint hostname, such as
.BR \%eus.codesigning.azure.net .
A URL is also accepted.
.TP
.BI \-\-account " name"
Artifact Signing account name.
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " name"
Certificate profile name.
.SS Sign options
.TP
.BI \-\-token " token"
Azure access token for the
.B \%https://codesigning.azure.net
resource; see
.BR AUTHENTICATION .
.TP
.BI \-\-oidc\-client\-id " id"
Client ID of an Entra app registration with a federated credential
trusting the GitHub Actions workflow; see
.BR AUTHENTICATION .
.TP
.BI \-\-oidc\-tenant\-id " id"
Tenant ID of that app registration.
.TP
.BI \-\-timestamp\-url " url"
RFC 3161 time-stamp authority, as a plain
.B http://
URL.
Default:
.B \%http://timestamp.acs.microsoft.com/timestamping/RFC3161
.TP
.B \-\-no\-timestamp
Do not timestamp.
Not recommended: Artifact Signing certificates are short-lived,
and an untimestamped signature becomes invalid when its certificate expires.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-parallel " n"
Sign at most
.I n
files concurrently.
Default: 8.
.TP
.BI \-\-dump\-cms " path"
Also write the DER-encoded CMS signature to
.I path
for inspection, such as with
.BR openssl\-asn1parse (1).
Only when signing a single file.
.SS Login options
.TP
.BI \-\-tenant " tenant"
Entra tenant to sign in to, as an ID or domain name.
The default is the aas\-sign author's own tenant,
so most users need this option.
.TP
.BI \-\-client\-id " id"
Entra application (client) ID to sign in with.
Default: \%04b07795\-8ddb\-461a\-bbee\-02f9e1bf7b46,
the Azure CLI's public client.
.SS General options
.B \-\-cacert
and
.B \-\-insecure
may appear anywhere and apply to any command.
.TP
.BI \-\-cacert " path"
Verify TLS servers against the PEM certificate bundle at
.IR path .
Ignored, with a warning, on Windows,
which always uses the system certificate store.
.TP
.B \-\-insecure
Disable TLS certificate verification, for diagnosing trust problems.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
.B sign
obtains an Azure access token from the first available of:
.IP 1. 4
.B \-\-token
or
.BR AZURE_ACCESS_TOKEN .
.IP 2. 4
GitHub Actions OIDC federation,
when both a client ID and a tenant ID are given,
by
.BR \-\-oidc\-client\-id " and " \-\-oidc\-tenant\-id
or, within such a job, by
.BR AZURE_CLIENT_ID " and " AZURE_TENANT_ID .
This works only in a job with
.B "id\-token: write"
permission;
elsewhere the options are an error.
.IP 3. 4
The refresh token cached by
.BR login .
If Entra rejects it as expired or revoked,
the cache is deleted and
.B login
must be run again.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AZURE_ACCESS_TOKEN
Access token used if
.B \-\-token
is not given.
.TP
.BR AZURE_CLIENT_ID ", " AZURE_TENANT_ID
Defaults for
.BR \-\-oidc\-client\-id " and " \-\-oidc\-tenant\-id ,
used only when
.B ACTIONS_ID_TOKEN_REQUEST_URL
is set.
.TP
.BR ACTIONS_ID_TOKEN_REQUEST_URL ", " ACTIONS_ID_TOKEN_REQUEST_TOKEN
Set by the GitHub Actions runner in jobs with
.B "id\-token: write"
permission, and required for OIDC federation.
.TP
.B SSL_CERT_FILE
PEM bundle of trusted CA certificates,
used if
.B \-\-cacert
is not given and the file exists.
Otherwise the first bundle found at a standard location, such as
.IR /etc/ssl/certs/ca\-certificates.crt ,
is used.
Ignored on Windows.
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " HOME
Locate the configuration directory, except on Windows.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/aas\-sign/
The configuration directory, or
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/aas\-sign/
if that is set, or
.I %APPDATA%\eaas\-sign\e
on Windows.
On POSIX it is created with mode 0700,
and the files in it are written with mode 0600.
.TP
.I config.json
Signing defaults, as a JSON object with optional
.BR endpoint ,
.BR account ,
and
.B profile
string members.
.TP
.I token\-cache.json
Refresh token written by
.B login
and updated by
.B sign
as Entra rotates it.
It can obtain access tokens as the signed-in user, so keep it private.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B aas\-sign
exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs,
including when any one of several files fails to sign.
.SH EXAMPLES
Sign in once, saving a signing target, then sign two files:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ aas\-sign login \-\-tenant contoso.com eus:contoso:release
$ aas\-sign sign app.exe plugin.dll
.fi
.RE
.PP
Sign with a different certificate profile, just this once:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ aas\-sign sign \-\-as eus:contoso:testing app.exe
.fi
.RE
.PP
Sign with an Azure CLI login instead:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ export AZURE_ACCESS_TOKEN="$(az account get\-access\-token \e
    \-\-resource https://codesigning.azure.net \e
    \-\-query accessToken \-o tsv)"
$ aas\-sign sign app.exe
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check the result:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ osslsigncode verify app.exe
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR osslsigncode (1),
.BR openssl\-asn1parse (1)
.PP
The project page,
.IR \%https://github.com/skeeto/aas\-sign ,
also documents the companion GitHub Action.
